#### Question 14:[cite: 4]
#### True or False: in R, mean(x) gives the same result as sum(x)/length(x).[cite: 4]
#### Concept: By definition, the arithmetic sample mean is the sum of observations divided by the sample size.
# Example verification in R:
x_test <- c(2, 4, 6, 8)
identical(mean(x_test), sum(x_test) / length(x_test))
#### Correct Answer: True[cite: 4]


